"wind_from_deg":[37.0,119.0]},"packet":{"draft_en":"On January 12, 2025, the Texas state monitor at HRM-16 Deer Park recorded 12.42 ppb of 1,3-butadiene in the 1:00 p.m. CST hour, against a 7-day median of 0.07 ppb. Wind there came from 119 degrees at 6.1 mph. 31 major permitted facilities lie in the upwind corridor. One of them, Intercontinental Terminals Deer Park Terminal, filed report 434494 for a release starting near that hour, but the report does not list 1,3-butadiene, so it does not match this reading. Requested follow-up: confirm what caused this 1,3-butadiene reading.","draft_es":"El 12 de enero de 2025, el monitor estatal de Texas en HRM-16 Deer Park registró 12.42 ppb de 1,3-butadieno en la hora de las 1:00 p. m. CST, frente a una mediana de 7 días de 0.07 ppb. El viento venía de 119 grados a 6.1 mph. Hay 31 instalaciones permitidas importantes en el corredor de donde venía el viento. Una de ellas, Intercontinental Terminals Deer Park Terminal, presentó el informe 434494 por una emisión que empezó cerca de esa hora, pero el informe no incluye 1,3-butadieno, así que no corresponde a esta lectura. Seguimiento solicitado: confirmar qué causó esta lectura de 1,3-butadieno.","drafted_by":"template (deterministic, no AI)","guard":{"passed":true,"rejected":[]}},"cannot_say":["A matching report is not proof the facility caused every reading; other sources can add to a spike.","'Not yet reported' is not a finding about any facility: Texas requires a report only at or above a reportable quantity, and air readings cannot measure how much was released (30 TAC 101.201).","The upwind corridor comes from wind direction at one monitor (geometry only), not a dispersion model; it cannot tell facilities along the same bearing apart.","Facility coordinates are as published by EPA ECHO and may be approximate.","Only regulator-grade monitors whose data the state publishes are used (including two industry-funded Houston Regional Monitoring sites), never low-cost sensors."],"p